  "faqAlarmsQIos": "How do I set up alarms, and what’s the notification permission?",
  "faqAlarmsAIos": "In Settings › Alarms, turn on “Alert before each shift”, choose how long before and, if you like, an alert the day before at a set time. In a day’s details you can remove its alarm with “No alarm this day”.\n\nWithout notification permission, Turnly can’t alert you. If the window to allow them doesn’t appear, turn them on in the system settings.",
  "faqWidgetAIos": "In Settings › Add widget you’ll see the sizes (small: today and tomorrow; medium: the next 7 days; large: the whole month) and how to place it. Touch and hold the home screen, tap the + at the top and look for Turnly.\n\nThe widget stores your upcoming days. The system decides when to update it and may delay the change of day. If it runs out of data, open Turnly to bring it up to date.",
  "faqBackupAIos": "Settings › Backup saves automatic backups on this device after each change, but they are lost if you lose it or uninstall the app. Export a file with “Export file” and save it to iCloud Drive or send it to yourself by WhatsApp or email.\n\nTo change devices: export the file, install Turnly on the new device, open the file with the app (or use “Import file” in Backup), and review the preview before restoring. “Test restore” checks that your latest backup can be fully recovered.",
  "calExportPermissionDeniedBodyIos": "Turn it on in the system settings (Turnly › Calendars) and come back here.",
  "backupUiWarningIos": "These backups are kept on this device. If you uninstall the app without another copy, it’s lost. Export a file and save it to iCloud Drive or send it by WhatsApp or email.",
  "backupUiExportSubtitleIos": "To save it to iCloud Drive or send it by WhatsApp or email",
  "settingsSectionHelp": "Help",
  "settingsHelpTitle": "Help and contact",
  "settingsHelpSubtitle": "Write to us if something isn’t working",
  "settingsHelpBody": "Questions, or something isn’t working? Tell us what’s happening and which version you use.",
  "settingsHelpSubtitleSoon": "We’re setting up the support email",
  "settingsHelpBodySoon": "We don’t have a support email yet. In the meantime, check the FAQ and, if something isn’t working, keep the version you use at hand.",
  "settingsHelpNoEmail": "The support email will arrive with the store version.",
  "settingsHelpCopyEmail": "Copy email",
  "settingsHelpCopyVersion": "Copy version",
  "settingsFaqTitle": "FAQ",
  "settingsFaqSubtitle": "Painting, rotations, alarms, widget and more",
  "faqIntro": "Quick answers about how Turnly works. Everything is on this device: no account or connection needed.",
  "faqNotFound": "Can’t find what you’re looking for?",
  "faqContact": "Help and contact",
  "faqPaintQ": "How do I paint the month?",
  "faqPaintA": "Tap “Paint” on the calendar, choose a shift at the bottom and tap the days or swipe across them. To empty a day, use “Erase”. Every stroke can be undone and redone with the arrows on the bar. Tap “Done” when you finish.\n\nIf you tap a day while you’re not painting, its details open: there you change the shift, add a note or go back to the pattern. If you touch and hold a day you start selecting several at once: you can set their shift, copy, cut and paste them, or repeat a week.",
  "faqPatternQ": "How do I apply a rotation, and what’s the offset?",
  "faqPatternA": "In paint mode, tap the “Pattern” button and follow the steps: choose your rotation (or create your own), the day you start and until when it repeats.\n\nThe offset is where in the cycle you are on the start day. If you’re on nights that day, in the step “Which day of the cycle are you on that day?” you tap the night and the rest adjusts itself. Days you’ve already changed by hand are kept or replaced, as you prefer. To end or remove a rotation, go to Settings › My rotations.",
  "faqDoubleQ": "How do I work a double shift?",
  "faqDoubleA": "A double is working two shifts on the same day. Tap the day and, in its details, use “Add a second shift”. If you’re painting, choose the “Add another shift” mode and tap the days. With several days selected, “Double with…” adds the shift to all of them.\n\nA day can have as many shifts as you need, and each one adds its own hours.",
  "faqPostNightQ": "What’s the automatic post-night?",
  "faqPostNightA": "It’s the rest on the day after a night. If you turn it on in Settings › Automatic post-night, when you paint or apply a night, the next day becomes Post-night if it was empty or off. Days that already had another shift aren’t touched. It’s off by default.",
  "faqNotesQ": "How do I use notes and the agenda?",
  "faqNotesA": "Tap a day and write in the note field; days with notes are marked on the calendar. Open the agenda at the top of the calendar: “Notes” lists your notes and custom holidays; “Shifts” shows upcoming shifts.\n\nSearch by text, regardless of case or accents, or by date: for example, 15/10 or Oct 15. Search covers all your notes and custom holidays, and shifts from one year ago to one year ahead.",
  "faqAlarmsQ": "How do I set up alarms, and what’s the exact alarms permission?",
  "faqAlarmsA": "In Settings › Alarms, turn on “Alert before each shift”, choose how long before and, if you like, an alert the day before at a set time. In a day’s details you can remove its alarm with “No alarm this day”.\n\nOn Android you need notifications and the “Alarms & reminders” permission in the system settings: without it, Android may delay the alert by a few minutes. The alarms screen tells you what’s missing and takes you to the settings. If your phone saves battery aggressively, set Turnly to unrestricted so it doesn’t stop the alerts.",
  "faqHolidaysQ": "How do I add a local holiday?",
  "faqHolidaysA": "In Settings › Holidays, choose your region and town to see the holidays that apply to you. If a local holiday is missing, tap that day on the calendar and turn on “Custom holiday”: give it a name and it counts as a holiday from then on.\n\nYou can also bring in holidays from your phone calendar in Settings › Holidays. Choose calendars and dates and review the preview: only all-day events are read, holidays you already have are skipped, and you can undo. Calendar events are never changed.",
  "faqWidgetQ": "How do I add the widget, and why does it change by itself?",
  "faqWidgetA": "In Settings › Add widget you’ll see the sizes (small: today and tomorrow; medium: the next 7 days; large: the whole month) and how to place it. On Android, touch and hold an empty area of the home screen, choose Widgets and look for Turnly.\n\nThe widget always shows today: it moves to the next day at midnight even if you don’t open the app, because it keeps your upcoming days stored. If you go a long time without opening Turnly, it runs out of data and asks you to open the app to catch up.",
  "faqBackupQ": "How do I back up and change devices?",
  "faqBackupA": "Settings › Backup saves automatic backups on this device after each change, but they are lost if you lose it or uninstall the app. Export a file with “Export file” and save it to Drive or send it to yourself by WhatsApp or email.\n\nTo change devices: export the file, install Turnly on the new device, open the file with the app (or use “Import file” in Backup), and review the preview before restoring. “Test restore” checks that your latest backup can be fully recovered.",
  "faqImportQ": "Can I import my shifts or export them to the calendar?",
  "faqImportA": "Yes. In Settings › Import shifts, you can bring in an LRHSoft «.Shifter» backup, shifts from your phone calendar, an .ics file or a CSV. In LRHSoft, create a backup in Menu › Backup › Local backup, then choose the file from Documents › ShifterBackups. Check the dates, shift types and preview before importing.\n\n“Export to phone calendar” copies your shifts once to a phone calendar. Exporting again does not duplicate them: only events created by Turnly are changed.",
  "faqCalendarsQ": "Can I keep several calendars and compare them?",
  "faqCalendarsA": "Yes. In Settings › Calendars you create one for your partner, a second job or a child: each one has its own rotations and days, and the shift types are shared. With two or more, the calendar name above the month lets you switch between them. The widget and the alarms follow the calendar marked “Widget and alarms”.\n\nTo see when you’re both off, tap “Compare calendars” on that same sheet: you choose two and see their shifts together and the days off you share in the month.",
  "faqSummaryQ": "How are hours and earnings calculated?",
  "faqSummaryA": "The summary icon on the calendar shows the shifts, hours, night hours and public holiday hours of the month, a whole year or the dates you choose in “Dates…” (up to 366 days). A shift counts on the day it starts, even if it crosses midnight.\n\nTo see amounts, set each shift type’s hourly rate and, if you have one, fixed allowance in Settings › My shifts. The estimate includes those fixed allowances, before tax, in the currency you pick in Settings › Appearance. It also adds the night and public holiday premiums per hour you set on each shift; the withholding only changes the net. In Settings › Hours and money you have allowance templates by sector, the closing day of your pay month and an overtime cap.\n\n“Shift allowance” is added once for each worked shift of that type, including split shifts; it does not depend on the hours. Rest days and absences do not add it.",
